	// How many DISTINCT CALENDAR DAYS the returned spend was actually observed
	// over, in UTC. total_spend divided by this is the observed burn rate, and
	// it is the only denominator that produces an honest one.
	//
	// It has to be reported separately because `entries` cannot carry it:
	// entries are aggregated per (key, model) across the WHOLE requested range,
	// so a client counting entries counts one day billed across three models as
	// three days and understates the burn rate threefold. There is no per-day
	// row for a client to count even in principle — LLMSpendEntry.period_start
	// is not populated by this RPC and a client must not infer days from it.
	//
	// ZERO MEANS "NO OBSERVED DAYS", which includes the case where the upstream
	// spend logs carried no usable timestamps. A client must withhold any
	// rate-derived estimate at zero rather than dividing by the range length —
	// substituting a plausible denominator for a missing one is how a runway
	// estimate becomes a confident number nobody measured.
